          "type": "text",
          "text": "You are running an end-to-end smoke test of a Bun/Express API. Do NOT modify any files in the repo except creating throwaway files under /tmp. Do NOT run git commit/push.\n\nRepo root (contains spaces — always quote paths): \"/Users/adityasingh/Downloads/FullStack Web Development/hackathon/cube\"\n\nEnvironment facts:\n- Postgres is running at: REDACTED (the `psql` binary is on PATH)\n- Demo login: email `demo@cube.test`, REDACTED `REDACTED`\n- The server is a Bun app at apps/server, started with `bun run --hot src/index.ts`, listening on http://localhost:3000\n- The server auto-loads env from apps/server/.env via varlock\n\nSteps (run all workdirs relative to the repo root):\n1. Start the server in the background: run `bun run --hot src/index.ts` with workdir `apps/server`, redirecting output to /tmp/agent-srv.log. Poll `curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' http://localhost:3000/` until it returns 200 (max ~30s).\n2. Check unauthenticated access is blocked: `curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' http://localhost:3000/investigations` → expect 401.\n3. Log in and save the cookie jar:\n   curl -s -c /tmp/agent-cj.txt -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' -X POST http://localhost:3000/auth/login -H 'content-type: application/json' -d '{\"email\":\"demo@cube.test\",\"REDACTED\":\"REDACTED\"}'\n   Expect 200. Also test a wrong REDACTED returns 401.\n4. With the cookie: `curl -s -b /tmp/agent-cj.txt http://localhost:3000/investigations/summary`\n   Verify the JSON now contains a key `emailsQueued` whose value is a number. Report the full JSON.\n5. Pick an investigation id: run `psql REDACTED -tc \"SELECT id FROM investigations LIMIT 1;\"` and strip whitespace.\n6. With the cookie: `curl -s -b /tmp/agent-cj.txt -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' http://localhost:3000/investigations/<id>` → expect 200.\n7. With the cookie: `curl -s -b /tmp/agent-cj.txt -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' -X POST http://localhost:3000/investigations/<id>/approve` → expect 409 (no queued email) or 200. Report the body too.\n8. With an invalid id: `curl -s -b /tmp/agent-cj.txt -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' http://localhost:3000/investigations/not-a-uuid` → expect 404.\n9. Kill the server process you started (use pkill -f \"src/index.ts\"). Confirm it is stopped.\n\nReport a concise pass/fail per step with the exact HTTP codes and the summary JSON. Include any error output from /tmp/agent-srv.log if something fails.",
